# ============================================================================
# SoyMutDB Portal (apps/web) — Cloudflare Pages custom headers
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Rules are matched per request path; a request inherits headers from ALL
# matching rules, and duplicate headers are comma-joined. Therefore `/*`
# below deliberately carries NO Cache-Control (it would merge with the
# /assets/* rule). Cache-Control is set only by the specific rules below.
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers — applied to every response (browsers ignore CSP on
# non-HTML responses, so applying it to assets is harmless).
# HSTS: Cloudflare Pages always serves HTTPS; max-age without
# includeSubDomains so the header never forces HTTPS on sibling subdomains
# (e.g. api.example.com, staging) that are not Cloudflare-fronted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://api.example.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src 'self' https://jbrowse.example.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hashed build assets (Vite emits everything under /assets/ with a content
# hash in the filename) — safe to cache immutable for 1 year.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HTML documents — always revalidate (same policy Cloudflare Pages sends by
# default; declared explicitly so it survives any future default change).
# Note: `/about`-style requests are served real SSG HTML by Pages itself;
# this rule matches the extensionless request path too via Pages' default
# no-cache behavior, so those pages never go stale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Placeholder domains to replace before going live (see deploy/cloudflare.md):
#   https://api.example.com      -> production API origin
#   https://jbrowse.example.com  -> deployed JBrowse origin (iframe on /browse)
# Keep the CSP in sync with the <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">
# in apps/web/index.html and apps/web/scripts/base-template.ts (SSG pages).
# Preview deployments: replace both occurrences with the STAGING origins.
# If VITE_CDN_ENABLED=true is ever re-enabled, add the CDN hosts to
# script-src here AND in the meta CSP.
# Cloudflare Web Analytics (C3): `https://static.cloudflareinsights.com`
# (script-src) and `https://cloudflareinsights.com` (connect-src) are listed
# statically so the beacon works whenever VITE_CLOUDFLARE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN is
# set at build time. Widening these origins is harmless when no token is set
# (the page simply never loads the beacon). The <meta> CSP in index.html is
# widened only when a token IS set (vite.config.ts transformIndexHtml) — the
# intersection of the two still allows the beacon in both cases.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
